            <ArticleTitle>Common ocular signs and symptoms in childhood.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>753-66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Children have many ocular complaints that generate a referral to the eye doctor. The complaints originate either from the child, the parents, the primary care physician, or teachers. This article describes the common complaints for which patients are referred and then how these problems should be addressed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
